# PHASE 15 — PERFORMANCE, ACCESSIBILITY, AND SECURITY

### Performance
- Reuse existing dependencies when possible.
- Avoid unnecessary packages.
- Optimize images and use responsive image sizes.
- Lazy-load noncritical images.
- Avoid blocking animations.
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders.
- Avoid repeated API calls.
- Show loading placeholders for slow operations.
- Keep mobile performance a priority.

### Accessibility
- Use semantic elements.
- Provide visible keyboard focus.
- Ensure sufficient color contrast.
- Associate labels with inputs.
- Provide meaningful error messages.
- Use keyboard-accessible menus and dialogs.
- Add accessible names to icon-only buttons.
- Respect reduced-motion settings.
- Do not communicate status through color alone.

### Security
- Keep credentials out of source code.
- Validate data at trust boundaries.
- Protect authenticated routes.
- Enforce server-side authorization.
- Avoid unsafe HTML rendering.
- Do not log passwords, tokens, or private guest information.
- Use secure handling for any uploaded files.
- Add rate limiting to sensitive public endpoints where supported.

